<title>NETHERLANDS: BZW cuts dredger Boskalis to Sell.</title>
<headline>BZW cuts dredger Boskalis to Sell.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (23/06)</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Boskalis	  Construction  38.50   Barclays Zoete Wedd</p>
<p>COMMENT: Sell (was Hold). Dredging demand increasing but capacity supply also accelerating due to Belgian new-build and jumbo hopper ordered by Japan's Penta Ocean. Latter represents stiff competition in the Far East, where demand is concentrated. Dutch and Belgian global dominance could be at stake. As such cycle set to peak in 1998, overcapacity seen pressuring prices in 1999.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS	 P/E    P/CF   Dividend p.s.</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     2.42	15.9   6.2    1.10</p>
<p>    1997		  3.00	12.8   5.5    1.30</p>
<p>    1998		  3.30	11.7   5.2    1.40</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
